---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
import { comparisonPairs } from '../../data/apps';
const pairs = comparisonPairs();
const path = "/compare";
const title = "Compare Shopify abandoned cart apps";
const desc = "Build a shortlist around cart events, purchase exits, channel ownership and measured contribution. Pairwise pages supply proposed checks, not observed merchant trials.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How should I choose two finalists?",
    "answer": "Start with the missing job: identifying cart abandoners, handing cart to checkout, or coordinating email and SMS. Require each finalist to demonstrate that job with your Shopify events."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Sequenzy beat Klaviyo on price or strategy?",
    "answer": "No winner is established here. Obtain current quotes at the same audience and send volume, demonstrate the required event integration, and record operator time and purchase exits."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should a tied comparison lead to a split stack?",
    "answer": "Only when the extra capability justifies another integration and queue. Assign channel ownership and verify purchase and opt-out suppression across providers before sending."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I select SMSBump or Yotpo Email & SMS now?",
    "answer": "Treat those legacy names as migration decisions. Yotpo announced Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025; its current SMS notice says the dashboard and background services are decommissioned."
  },
  {
    "question": "How long should a comparison run?",
    "answer": "Choose duration and holdout allocation from order volume, conversion delay and detectable effect. A fourteen-day pilot or five-percent holdout is not a validated universal design."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16"><div class="container"><h1 class="hero-title">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">{desc}</p>

<TldrBox title="Choose the decision first" picks={[
{label:'Event handoff',tool:'Klaviyo vs Omnisend',reason:'Inspect cart identification, checkout transition and purchase exits in each setup.'},
{label:'Capture handoff',tool:'Omnisend vs Privy',reason:'Follow signup permission and welcome offers into recovery without duplicate discounts.'},
{label:'Legacy names',tool:'Yotpo / SMSBump',reason:'Use replacement guidance; the retired email/SMS service is not a new purchase option.'}
]} />
<article class="prose-shopify card mt-12 p-8">
<h2>Compare the job, then the interface</h2>
<p>Use <a href="/apps">the app directory</a> to identify candidates and <a href="/guides">the guides</a> to define timing and incentive rules. This hub supplies a repeatable selection process. A feature-table checkmark cannot prove that a purchase cancels an already queued reminder or that one provider sees another provider’s opt-out.</p>
<h2>Write an event contract</h2>
<p>Record what starts recovery, which shopper can be identified, and what ends it. Separate adding to cart from starting checkout. Require evidence for the cart items, variant, quantity, return URL and order ID. Set an acceptable event delay from your operating needs, then inspect the event and queue timestamps rather than assuming a native integration is instantaneous.</p>
<h2>Four proposed acceptance exercises</h2>
<p>First, abandon a mixed-SKU cart and change its quantity before the next step: inspect the resulting items and destination. Second, advance from cart to checkout and confirm the lower-intent flow exits. Third, purchase while a message is waiting and inspect every sender’s remaining queue. Fourth, make a variant unavailable and check what the reminder and return link actually offer. These are exercises for your team; no completed test or recovery lift is asserted here.</p>
<h2>Choose channel ownership before a split stack</h2>
<p>A capture tool, email provider and SMS provider can be combined, but more tools add synchronization work. Name one owner for each stage and channel. Test welcome/cart coupon overlap, repeat checkout, opt-out propagation and a purchase between email and SMS. Compare that maintenance burden with a single-provider design before deciding whether the additional capability is worthwhile.</p>
<h2>Normalize quotes and operating effort</h2>
<p>Give finalists the same eligible audience, monthly email sends, SMS destinations, expected growth and required automation access. Include implementation, support and ongoing maintenance in the budget. Verify current billing definitions; this hub does not establish a pay-per-email model or retainer saving for any vendor. Record who can safely edit the workflow and how a failed edit is rolled back.</p>
<h2>Measure contribution with uncertainty</h2>
<p>Separate platform-attributed revenue from incremental orders. If feasible, randomize eligible customers into mutually exclusive treatment and no-message groups, with a duration and allocation justified by traffic and conversion delay. Compare contribution per eligible customer after discounts, goods, fulfillment, payment, message and return costs. Deduplicate orders across senders. A revenue tie within uncertainty supplies no evidence that either tool is superior.</p>
<h2>Keep a dated decision record</h2>
<p>Use a scorecard agreed before the trial: required events, purchase exits, permission handling, inventory behavior, cost and operator effort. Treat failed essential controls as launch blockers rather than averaging them away with attractive templates. Save evidence, unresolved limits, quote date and rollback owner. Revisit when catalog, markets or channel ownership changes.</p>
<h2>Read legacy comparisons as replacement decisions</h2>
<p>Yotpo’s <a href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">migration announcement</a> scheduled Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. The <a href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">current SMS notice</a> confirms decommissioning. Checked November 25, 2026. Retained records may support a rebuild; access to an old dashboard or export is not promised.</p>
</article>
<div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">{pairs.map(([a,b]) => <a class="card recovery-card" href={`/compare/${a.slug}-vs-${b.slug}`}><h2>{a.name} vs {b.name}</h2><p>Workflow evaluation and migration context</p></a>)}</div>

<FaqSection faqs={faqs} /></div></section></BaseLayout>
